    material_mask.lua
        1→---@meta soluna.material.mask
        3→---
        4→--- Soluna material mask module
        5→---
        7→---@class soluna.material.mask
        8→local matmask = {}
        11→--- Creates a colored mask sprite.
        12→---
        13→--- Color format: ARGB as 32-bit integer 0xAARRGGBB.
        14→--- If the alpha byte is 00 it is forced to 0xFF (fully opaque).
        15→---
        16→---@param sprite integer 1-based sprite index (will be stored as 0-based internally)
        17→---@param color  integer Color in ARGB format (0xAARRGGBB, e.g. 0xFF00FF00 for opaque green)
        18→---@return userdata mask Binary blob containing the packed mask_primitive; push it as a Lua string
        19→function matmask.mask(sprite, color) end
        21→return matmask
